{"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"],"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let store = try SegmentStore()","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, with one "},{"code":"write()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss too ("},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as the app moves to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"background or terminates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and so is one whose event’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"encode(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" throws."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What is kept.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Every event "},{"code":"DiscoveredEvent.all","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists, the "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" structs of every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module the program links and the library’s own, or only the "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" types in "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other, are never written, and are lost if the app ends first. The first record of each such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type is reported as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so a type left out by mistake,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as one that conforms to "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand, shows up."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level "},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as its span ended with the earlier run."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Deleting.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. A segment kept for one undelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record keeps its delivered ones too. Only recovery rewrites a segment: one still holding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records after it drops some ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":") is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rewritten without them, so each drop is reported once. Should the rewrite fail, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"segment is kept as it was and the next launch reports those drops again."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading back."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" When a destination’s full buffer drops a batch on its way through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, the delivery reads that batch’s records back from the log once the destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has caught up, reading each segment they are in once, and hands them to it in this run,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each in the context it was tracked in, which the delivery keeps. A record the bound dropped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before the read finished isn’t read back, and one that can’t be read or decoded is logged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and waits for a later launch."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The log never holds more than ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered yields a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports"},{"text":". A record too large for an empty log","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is kept in memory only.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes back with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Other versions.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changed event types."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional one added since is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored at another ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event.schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store share its log."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentStore.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L72"},"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SegmentStore","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"],"title":"Stores","generated":true,"anchor":"Stores"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/defaultDirectory":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a store keeps its segments unless it is given a directory."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/defaultdirectory","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultDirectory","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV","text":"FilePath","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"defaultDirectory"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/takeRecoveredRecords()":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"takeRecoveredRecords()","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/takerecoveredrecords()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The records of the segments earlier runs left, oldest first, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each one a delivery had started on; later calls return none."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"takeRecoveredRecords","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/append(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"record","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the log before returning, when its event type is one of ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fits the bound.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/append(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"append","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"append(_:)"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/defaultByteBound":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"defaultByteBound","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/defaultbytebound","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bound a store has unless it is given another: 5 MiB (5,242,880 bytes)."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultByteBound"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound"},"doc://Persistence/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing "},{"code":"recordCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" records, tracked within "},{"code":"timestamps","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", to disk failed (the disk is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full, say, or segments that couldn’t be deleted fill the bound), so they are kept in memory"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only: delivered in this run if it lasts long"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enough, lost if it ends first."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/writefailed(recordcount:timestamps:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"writeFailed"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"recordCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"timestamps"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SN","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ClosedRange"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Date"},{"kind":"text","text":">)"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"DropReport.writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"DropReport.versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/versionmismatch(event:storedversion:currentversion:recordcount:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery read "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordCount"},{"type":"text","text":" intact records of the event named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"},{"type":"text","text":" stored at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"storedVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", while the store’s type of that name is at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":"), and dropped them without decoding them: the version changed for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change their bytes can’t be read through. Reported once per segment, or per database, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each event and stored version, by the event’s name and then the stored version."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"versionMismatch"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"event"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"storedVersion"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"currentVersion"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"recordCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","role":"symbol","title":"RecordStore","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"title":"DropReport","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/pendingRecordCount":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/pendingrecordcount","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"pendingRecordCount","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"pendingRecordCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"abstract":[{"text":"How many records the log keeps that are not yet delivered.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStoreError":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStoreError"}],"title":"SegmentStoreError","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstoreerror","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The error ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" throws: an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"argument it can’t open a store with, or the file system’s failure.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStoreError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError"},"doc://Persistence/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/notPersisted(event:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/notpersisted(event:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"DropReport.notPersisted(event:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"key